289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-02-23T09:07:52Z","updated_at":"2025-02-23T20:06:41Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.2 - 4.4-dev1. Have not tested other ones, but would assume it is an old problem.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.rc1 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7216) - AMD Ryzen 7 3700X 8-Core Processor (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf you reimport 3d model (on which you have made physical bones on) while animation is playing, then positions of physical bones get messed up. You can press \"Show rest only\" to avoid the problem, but it is very easy to forget and you are gonna have to reposition all of your physical bones again...\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. create physical skeleton\n2. choose any animation to play\n3. reimport the model\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[skeleton-import-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18929281/skeleton-import-test.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103206/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103206/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}